  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1028 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nA 595 dam ridge is centered over the Southern Plains and Lower\nMississippi Valley, with shortwave energy bypassing the region\nwell to the north. Surface analysis shows a broad 1020 mb high\npressure system across the eastern CONUS. This high will remain\nstationary through the week, maintaining a persistent return flow\nthat will gradually transport higher moisture into the Mid-South.\n\nPersistent ridging will drive a steady increase in daily\ntemperatures and humidity. Areas along and west of the\nMississippi River have a medium-to-high chance of reaching 100F \ndaily, with heat indices ranging from 103F to 110F across the \nregion. Oppressive heat will initially target western areas before\nexpanding across the entire Mid-South by midweek. As such, a Heat\nAdvisory is in effect on Monday and there is high confidence that\ndaily heat headlines will be required through Friday.\n\nGuidance suggests easterly waves may undercut the ridge late this\nweek, potentially triggering isolated thunderstorms; however,\nmeaningful heat relief is unlikely. Predominantly hot and dry\nconditions will persist, elevating the risk for rapid-onset\ndrought. A medium signal remains for a backdoor cold front late\nthis weekend, which could eventually moderate the heat and\nhumidity.",
